id=a52sxq_wifi_weak_networks
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: weak Wi-Fi networks show in the Wi-Fi list
author=kusti420
description=Samsung's wifitrackerlib (com.samsung.android.wifitrackerlib.SemWifiEntryFilter, inlined ScanResultUpdater loop in WifiPickerTracker.updateWifiEntries) drops every scan result below -78 dBm (2.4 GHz, also 6 GHz) or -75 dBm (5 GHz) before it becomes a list entry; only the connected BSSID is kept. A tester saw 1 of ~21 nearby networks. Owner decision 2026-11-08: show them so they can be connected to. This sets the cut to -88 dBm on all bands (0x58), the first step of config_wifiRssiLevelThresholds (-88/-82/-74/-63 in WifiRROverlayApp), so the weakest shown network has one bar. Patched in both copies: SecSettings (Settings > Connections > Wi-Fi) and SystemUI (quick panel Wi-Fi list); no other APK/JAR in the image carries the filter. Also the default level (index 1) of the hidden Wi-Fi Labs list filter (Settings.Global sec_wifi_developer_rssi_level, only read when sem_wifi_developer_option_visible=1) gets -88; its strong (-73/-70) and all (-127) levels stay. semForceScan's min(..., -80/-77) for short lists becomes a no-op. NOT changed on purpose: auto-join / network selection (config_wifi_framework_wifi_score_entry_rssi_threshold_24GHz -78, _5GHz -75, 6 GHz -81 in WifiRROverlayApp; WifiNetworkSelector.isSignalTooWeak, PNO min RSSI, WakeupEvaluator), so the phone does not jump onto a -88 dBm network by itself; manual connect (WifiManager.connect) has no RSSI gate in service-wifi or semwifi-service. Also unchanged: semwifi-service ScanPool.isAllowToShowInScanList (-80/-77, only feeds the "Wi-Fi networks available" notification), SemWifiConnectivityMonitor poor-link heuristics ("Switch to mobile data" setting).
